# AXOM accounts (optional). Copy to web/.env.local and fill in your Supabase
# project's PUBLIC values (Dashboard → Project Settings → API Keys). The
# publishable key (sb_publishable_…) is designed to ship in client code —
# row-level security in supabase/migrations protects every row. The legacy
# anon key also works via VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY. Never put a secret or
# service-role key here. Set the same two values in Vercel for hosted builds.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://jofkmfwkidubxcutkwzf.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
